      "chunks": [
        "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) Collaboration\nCollaboration with Germany\n1. Anhalt University of Applied Sciences\nYear of establishment: 2002\nScope: This is a teacher student exchange program exists between Anhalt University, Germany and MPBME department since March, 2002. Main goal of this collaboration is to develop medical physics education and research in Bangladesh\n2. German Cancer Research Centre (DKFZ,)Heidelberg University\nScope: A Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed between MPBME department, Gono University and Heidelberg University. Students, who have outstanding result, get opportunity to do M.Sc in this university every year. Also, Ph.D students get opportunity to perform their practical work in this university.\n3. Mannheim University Hospital (UMM), Mannheim\nYear of establishment: 2012\nScope:\nTo establish a scientific collaboration and exchange programme on various levels\nCollaboration and exchange in scientific research and development\nSetting up a full-fledged laboratory and workshops for practical work",
        "Transfer of innovative health care technology into Bangladesh’s hospitals and industry as well as transfer of the specific demands of Bangladesh as a developing country into education, research and development\nExchange personnel on all academic levels: university professors, lectures, graduate students, research scientists at PhD level\nMake joint efforts to obtain funding and support for education, teacher-student exchange, development, projects in research, establishment of laboratories and workshops from national and international agencies and institutions as well as industrial companies.\nThrough the renewed agreement with Germany by 2018-2021, skilled manpower will be created for cancer treatment in Bangladesh and other South Asian countries.\nCollaboration with China\n1. Jiliang University\nYear of establishment: 2016\nScope: Top ranked graduate students get chance to participate in this medical physics co-operative research program. They get advanced training in medical physics, biomedical engineering and computer sciences.\n2. Zhejiang Cancer Hospital\nYear of establishment: 2017\nJoint Research Projects and Thesis\nTraining Program\nPost Graduate Internship/ Fellowship",
        "Visiting Faculty members\nCollaboration with India\n1. North Bengal Oncology Center, Siliguri, India\nScope: Students get opportunity to perform the practical part of Bachelor, Master and Ph.D thesis under this collaboration. Faculty members from both institutions visit each other to develop medical physics in both institutions.\n2.Saroj Gupta Cancer Center and Research Institute,Thakurpukur, Kolkata, India\nYear of establishment: 2011\nScope: In the frame of a sandwich program every year students get opportunity to do joint research and thesis in this institutions.\n3. Narayana Superspeciality Hospital, (NSH) kolkata, India\nYear of establishment:2019\nPractical classes for bachelor and master students\nJoint academic activities such as joint conference, seminar and hands-on training program for medical physicists and medical doctors and technicians and nurses\nJoint research programs (project/ thesis for bachelor, master and Ph. D students)\nJoint health care personnel training programs\nExchange of staff and students\nCollaboration with Srilanka\nDepartment of Nuclear Science, Faculty of Science, University of Colombo, Srilanka.\nCollaboration with Pakistan",
        "Department of Physics, University of Karachi, Pakistan."
