        "Course Plan\nCourse Curriculum\nThe course curriculum for B.Sc. (Honours) in Chemistry has been prepared with the general education courses conducted by the other relevant departments and core courses that characterize the discipline/department.\nDuration of the program: 8 Semesters, 4 Years.\nAdmission Requirements: A student intending to pursue the course for the B.Sc. (Honours) in Physics may be admitted provided she/he has passed the S.S.C. and H.S.C. (or A Level) examinations with required grades (minimum GPA-2.5 in each) with Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry.\nTotal minimum credit requirement to complete the program: 148 (according to BNQF (Part B) for Higher Education).\nTotal class weeks in each semester: 18 weeks / semester.\nMinimum CGPA requirements for graduation: CGPA 2.00\nMaximum academic years of completion: 6 years\nCategory of Courses:\nGeneral Education Courses: Interdisciplinary courses, beyond the discipline/program, that provides a well-rounded learning experience to the students of an academic program) such as Arts and Humanities, Social Sciences, ICT, Basic Science/STEM etc. (as applicable for the discipline/academic program)."
