      "chunks": [
        "Profile\nMd. Golam Mostofa\nAssistant Professor\nQualification: B. Pharm, M. Pharm (University of Rajshahi)\nMobile: +8801744719417\nE-mail: gm.sajol@gmail.com, mostofa.pharmacy@gonouniversity.edu.bd\nShort Biography\nEducation\nExperiences\nAdministrative Services\nPublications\nGrants\nEditorial Board/Reviewer\nConferences\nTraining\nMembership\nAwards and Achievements\nMd. Golam Mostofa is a registered A-grade Pharmacist in Bangladesh with expertise in pharmacy and pharmaceutical sciences. He began his career at ACI Limited as a Product Executive, gaining experience in marketing, product launches, and data analysis.\nHe later joined GONO BISHWABIDYALAY as a Lecturer and is currently an Assistant Professor in the Department of Pharmacy. He teaches and supervises B. Pharm and M. Pharm students, guiding them in research methodology and critical analysis. His research focuses on phytochemistry, anticancer studies, and Computer-Aided Drug Design (CADD).\nORCiD ResearchGate Google Scholar LinkedIn\nHe earned his Master of Pharmacy (M. Pharm) degree from the University of Rajshahi in 2017.\nHe completed his Bachelor of Pharmacy (B. Pharm Honours) from the University of Rajshahi in 2015.",
        "He passed the Higher Secondary Certificate (H.S.C.) from Fulbari Government College, Dinajpur, under the Dinajpur Board in 2010.\nHe completed the Secondary School Certificate (S.S.C.) from Fulbari G.M. Pilot High School, Dinajpur, under the Rajshahi Board in 2008.\nHe served as a Lecturer in the Department of Pharmacy at Gono Bishwabidyalay from March 1, 2020 to July 28, 2025.\nHe served as a Product Executive at ACI Limited from October 28, 2018 to February 29, 2020, working in the Product Management Department at the company’s Gulshan, Dhaka office, where he was involved in product planning, coordination, and marketing-related activities.\nJournal Publications\nAzim Uddin, A.S.M. Ali Reza, Adeeba Anjum, Md. Aziz Abdur Rahman, Samina Yesmin, Mst Samima Nasrin, Lima Khatun, Md. Golam Mostofa, Md. Golam Sadik and A.H.M. Khurshid Alam. In vitro Cytotoxic and Anti-ROS Potentials of the Aerial Part of Pyrrosia lanceolata on A549 Cells and Cell Free Condition. Bangladesh Pharmaceutical Journal. 2024; 27(2): 137-148. DOI: 10.3329/bpj.v27i2.75182",
