        "Abdul Rahim*, Md. Golam Mostofa*, Md. Golam Sadik, Md. Aziz Abdur Rahman, Md. Ibrahim Khalil, Toshifumi Tsukahara, KyoKo Nakagawa-Goto and AHM Khurshid Alam. The anticancer activity of two glycosides from the leaves of Leea aequata L. Natural Product Research. 2020; 35(24): 5867-5871. DOI: 10.1080/14786419.2020.1798661\nMahbubur Rahman, A. S. M. Sakhawat Hossain, Md. Golam Mostofa, Muhammad Ali Khan, Rezwan Ali, Ashik Mosaddik, Md. Golam Sadik and A. H. M. Khurshid Alam. Evaluation of anti-ROS and anticancer properties of Tabebuia pallida L. Leaves. Clinical Phytoscience. 2019; 5:17. DOI: 10.1186/s40816-019-0111-5\nRokshana Sharmin, Maruf-ul-Islam, Md. Hasibul Hasan Joarder, Md. Mohiuddin Alamgir, Md. Golam Mostofa and A. H. M. Khurshid Alam. Antidiabetic and Hepatoprotective Activities of Bombax ceiba Young Roots in Alloxan-Induced Diabetic Mice. Journal of Nutritional Health and Food Science. 2018; 6(5):1-7. DOI: 10.15226/jnhfs.2018.001140",
        "Samima Nasrin, Md. Golam Mostofa, Md. Harun-Or-Rashid, Md. Shofiqul Islam and A. H. M. Khurshid Alam. Antioxidant, free radical scavenging, antibacterial and cytotoxic compound from the leaves of Syzygium fruticosum. International Journal of Pharma Sciences and Scientific Research. 2018; 4:6.\nConference Publications\nOral Presentation\nMd. Golam Mostofa and AHM Khurshid Alam. The apoptosis-inducing antiproliferative activity and quantitative phytochemical profiling of polyphenol-rich part of Leea aequata L. leaves. Conference Title: International Conference on Science and Technology for Celebrating the Birth Centenary of Bangladesh. Date: March 11-13, 2021. Place: BCSIR, Dhaka, Bangladesh.\nPoster Presentation\nFarhad Hossain, Md. Golam Mostofa and AHM Khurshid Alam. Anti-proliferative and antioxidant potentials of bioactive edible vegetable fraction of Achyranthes ferruginea Roxb. in cancer cell line. Conference Title: International Conference on Science and Technology for Celebrating the Birth Centenary of Bangladesh. Date: March 11-13, 2021. Place: BCSIR, Dhaka, Bangladesh.",
        "Md. Golam Mostofa, Joy Sarker and AHM Khurshid Alam. Anticancer and Apoptosis inducing Effects of 7-0-methylmearnsitrin and Roseoside A in Different Cancer Cell Lines. Conference Title: Bangladesh Chemical Society Conference-2019. Date: November 9-10, 2019. Place: University of Rajshahi, Rajshahi-6205, Bangladesh.\nMd. Golam Mostofa, Joy Sarker and AHM Khurshid Alam. Isolation and identification of compounds from bioactive fraction of Leea aequata leaves as an antioxidant and free radical scavenger agent. Conference Title: Translational Research in Biochemistry for Better Life and Sustainable Development. Date: September 6, 2018. Place: Senate Bhaban, University of Rajshahi, Rajshahi-6205, Bangladesh.\nMd. Golam Mostofa, Md. Mahbubur Rahman, ASM Sakhawat Hossain and AHM Khurshid Alam. Antioxidant and Anticancer Properties of Tabebuia pallida L. Leaves. Conference Title: Ethnopharmacology and Drug Development: Innovation meets Tradition. Date: January 13-15, 2018. Place: Nabab Nawab Ali Chowdhury Senate Bhaban, Dhaka University, Bangladesh.",
        "Md. Golam Mostofa, Md Mahbubur Rahman, ASM Sakhawat Hossain and AHM Khurshid Alam. Apoptogenic effect of antioxidant enriched-leaves of Tabebuia pallida in EAC cells. Conference Title: Ethnopharmacology and Drug Development: Innovation meets Tradition. Date: January 13-15, 2018. Place: Nabab Nawab Ali Chowdhury Senate Bhaban, Dhaka University, Bangladesh.\nHe participated in the International Conference on Science and Technology for Celebrating the Birth Centenary of Bangladesh, organized by Bangladesh Council of Scientific and Industrial Research (BCSIR), held at BCSIR, Dhaka, from March 11–13, 2021.\nHe attended the Bangladesh Chemical Society Conference-2019, held at the University of Rajshahi, from November 9–10, 2019.\nHe participated in the conference titled “Translational Research in Biochemistry for Better Life and Sustainable Development”, held at the University of Rajshahi on September 6, 2018.",
        "He attended the 18th International Congress of the International Society for Ethnopharmacology & 5th International Congress of the Society for Ethnopharmacology, India, organized by the Department of Pharmacy, University of Dhaka, held at the University of Dhaka, from January 13–15, 2018.\nHe also participated in a seminar on “Laboratory Safety”, organized by ESCO, held at the University of Rajshahi on February 20, 2017.\nHe participated in the “Habits of Highly Effective People: Personal Effectiveness (H1–H2)” training organized by ACI Limited in Tejgaon, Dhaka, on November 5, 2019, focusing on personal and professional effectiveness skills.\nHe completed the “TOT for Marketer” training conducted by ACI Limited in Tejgaon, Dhaka, on March 23, 2019, aimed at enhancing marketing and training competencies.\nHe attended a “Selling Skill Workshop” organized by ACI Limited in Tejgaon, Dhaka, from March 12–14, 2019, strengthening practical sales and communication skills.\nHe successfully completed “MS Excel Level-1” training at ACI Limited, Gulshan, Dhaka, on February 19, 2019, developing professional data management and analytical skills.",
        "He participated in “Bioinformatics and Drug Design: Hands-on Training” organized by the IEEE Student Branch, Rajshahi University, at Rajshahi University, on February 10, 2018, gaining practical exposure to computational drug design.\nHe completed “Training on Biosafety and Biosecurity” conducted by icddr,b in Mohakhali, Dhaka, from January 6–7, 2017, focusing on laboratory safety and biosecurity practices.\nHe undertook In-Plant Training at Beximco Pharmaceutical Ltd., Gazipur, from June 15–28, 2016, acquiring practical industrial experience in pharmaceutical manufacturing and operations.\nHe is a registered A-grade Pharmacist of the Bangladesh Pharmacy Council, holding Registration Number A13076/17.\nHe secured the Second Position in the “First Scientific Poster Presentation–2024,” organized by Gono Bishwabidyalay.\nHe became a Semi-finalist in the Microsoft Excel–based competition titled “Magic Cell Maestro – 2020,” organized by ACI Limited and held in 2020, demonstrating advanced data handling and spreadsheet analysis skills."
