      "chunks": [
        "Profile\nProfessor Niranjan Biswas\nHead of the Department\nQualification: B.A. (Honours), M.A. (Dhaka University)\nMobile: 01711372897\nE-mail: profnbiswas1965@gmail.com\nShort Biography\nEducation\nExperiences\nAdministrative Services\nPublications\nGrants\nEditorial Board/Reviewer\nConferences\nTraining\nMembership\nAwards and Achievements",
        "Niranjan Biswas was born at Harirampur of Manikganj district in 1965. He passed the SSC and HSC examinations respectively from Dakshin Chandpur High School, Harirampur and Govt. Debendra College, Manikganj. He completed his BA (Hons) and MA from English Department of Dhaka University. He qualified in the BCS examination and joined the Education Cadre as Lecturer in English in 1993. Completing Departmental examinations and the Senior Scale examinations, he got promoted as Assistant Professor and Associate Professor. Then he completed the Advanced Course on Education and Management. In 2017, he was promoted as Professor of English and finished the Senior Staff Course on Education and Management. In 2024, his Leave Preparatory Retirement began and he joined Gono Bishwabidyalay, Savar, Dhaka as Professor of English. He visited Singarpore, Malaysia, Indonesia, Bhutan and India for different academic purposes.\nExamination | Year of passing | Group/Subject | Board/University | Results- Division/Class\nS S C | 1980 | Arts | Dhaka Board | 1st\nH S C | 1982 | Arts | Dhaka Board | 1st\nB A (Honours) | 1985 | English | Dhaka University | 2nd\nM A | 1986 | English | Dhaka University | 2nd",
        "Period | Designation | Institutions\nAugust 2017 – Present | Professor, English | Bhawal Badre Alam Govt. College, Gazipur.\nAugust 2006 – August 2017 | Associate Professor, English | (i) Bhawal Badre Alam Govt. College, Gazipur;\n(ii) Tongi Govt. College, Gazipur;\n(iii) Ghior Govt. College, Manikganj.\nJanuary 2023 – August 2006 | Assistant Professor, English | (i) Govt. Debendra College, Manikganj;\n(ii) Kazipur Govt. Monsur Ali College, Sirajganj.\nNovember 1993 – January 2003 | Lecturer, English | (i) Muminunnisa Govt. Mohila College, Mymensingh;\n(ii) Lakshmipur Govt. College, Lakshmipur;\n(iii) Bhawal Badre Alam Govt. College, Gazipur;\n(iv) Char Bhadrsan Govt. College, Faridpur.\nExperience as Head of the Department:\nWorked as Head of the Department of Honours and Master’s teaching Deaprtment of English at Tongi Govt. College, Gazipur (2007-2013) and at Bhawal Badre Alam Govt. College (2013-Present) and performing the duties/responsibilities, such as –\nOrganizing, processing and monitoring the activities for admission/enrolment at BA (Honours 1st Year), Master’s (Preliminary) and Master’s (Final Year) of as many as 350 students in every academic year.",
        "Preparing class-routine at the Honours and Master’s levels’ adjusting with the Higher Secondary and Degree (Pass) levels classes of the institution, assigning the classes to the teachers of the Department and ensuring and monitoring all their classes of different levels.\nEvaluating the performance of the Lecturers, Assistant Professors and Associate Professors working at the Department annually in their A C Rs.\nOrganizing and monitoring the in-course examinations (evaluation on 20 marks for each paper) including preparing question papers, conducting the examinations, examining the scripts and preparing results to send online to add to the National University’s final transcript.\nOrganizing and presiding over the Viva-voce examinations for Honours 4th Year and Master’s Final Year’s final examinations.\nOrganizing the question-setting, examining scripts and preparing results of all internal tests.",
        "Organizing and managing to arrange excursion for the students of the Department every year, arranging and presiding over seminars with the participation of the students and the teachers of the Department and supervising and evaluating the preparation and presentation of term-paper of the Master’s Final Year students.\nOperating (jointly with the Principal) the bank account of the seminar of the Department maintaining the expenditures as per financial rules and getting those annually audited by the public auditors.\n01. Working as a member of the Editorial Board of the Journal of Gono Bishwabidyalay (ISSN: 2521-828X)\n02. Worked as editor of the magazine Protibhash, Bhawal Badre Alam Govt. College, Gazipur in 2018.\n03. Worked as editor of the souvenir of EPD Training Course at NAEN in 2018.\nSeminars –\na) Attended seminars in Bhutan and Malaysia respectively in the years of 2016 and 2018.\nb) Arranged and presided over seminars/webinars of the Department of English, Bhawal Badre Alam Govt. College, Gazipur on the topics like – Imperialism and Colonialism in The Tempest, The Conditions Set by Virginia Woolf for the Promotion of Creative Genius.\nWorkshops –",
        "Organized and worked as the presenter at NAEM, Dhaka as a member of the workshop committee during the trainings of ACEM and SSCEM.\nTitle of the Training | Source of fund/Institution | Commencement of training | End of training\nFoundation Training | GoB\nNAEM, Dhaka | 28/01/1995 | 28/03/1995\nHigher Training Course for the Teachers | GoB\nNational University, Gazipur | 15/05/2005 | 28/06/2005\nProject Management | GoB\nNAEM, Dhaka | 25/08/2008 | 31/08/2008\nAdvanced Course on Education and Management (ACEM) | GoB\nNAEM, Dhaka | 24/04/2016 | 07/06/2016\n3 Week Training on Public Procurement Management | GoB\nCPTU, IMED, Ministry of Planning | 31/12/2016 | 16/01/2017\nSenior Staff Course on Education and Management (SSCEM) | GoB\nNAEM, Dhaka | 01/06/2018 | 14/08/2018\nEducational Planning and Development (EPD) Training Course | GoB\nNAEM, Dhaka | 05/11/2018 | 04/12/2018\nStudy Tour abroad: India, Bhutan, Malaysia, Indonesia, Singapore.\n01. Life member of Dhaka University Alumni Association.\n02. Life member of Jagannath Hall Alumni Association, The University of Dhaka.\n03. Member of BELTA."
      ]
