        "Profile\nProfessor Dr Md Nurul Islam\nAdjunct Faculty\nQualification: Ph. D.\nMobile: 01552300568\nE-mail: head.mpbme@gonouniversity.edu.bd / mnislam004@yahoo.com\nAreas of Interest\nShort Biography\nEducation\nExperiences\nAdministrative Services\nPublications\nGrants\nEditorial Board/Reviewer\nConferences\nTraining\nMembership\nAwards and Achievements\nName of Degree | Group/Subject | Years of Passing | Board/ Institute\nS.S.C. | Science | 1978 | Comilla Board\nH.S.C. | Science | 1980 | Comilla Board\nB.Sc. (Hons.) | Physics | 1984 | Jahangirnagar University\nM.Sc. (Thesis) | Physics | 1985 | Jahangirnagar University\nM. Phil. | Physics (Neutron Radiography | 2000 | Jahangirnagar University\nPh. D. | Physics (Neutron Radiography) | 2006 | Jahangirnagar University\nCareer History\nDuration | Summary\n06 Nov 2022 – Present | Head, Department of Medical Physics and Biomedical Engineering, Gono Bishwabidyalay. Leading academic and administrative activities in the department.\n➤ Organizing curriculum development, faculty development, interdisciplinary collaboration, and research initiatives in medical physics and biomedical engineering.",
        "01 Jan 2021 | Post-Retirement Leave (PRL) after serving as Director General, Atomic Energy Research Establishment (AERE). Officially retired under government regulations.\n➤ Concluded over 30 years of service in nuclear research and national research leadership.\n25 Sept 2019 – 31 Dec 2020 | Director General & Chief Scientific Officer, Atomic Energy Research Establishment (AERE), BAEC, Savar, Dhaka.\n➤ Responsible for overall leadership, strategic planning, management of multidisciplinary research & development, administrative and financial programs.\n03 Mar 2014 – 24 Sep 2019 | Director & Chief Scientific Officer, Training Institute, AERE. Supervised training programs and scientific development.\n➤ Initiated updated training curricula to align with international nuclear standards.\n27 Jul 2011 – 02 Mar 2014 | Chief Scientific Officer & Group Leader, NR Group, RNPD, INST. Directed neutron radiography research & development and led project teams.\n➤ Led major experiments enhancing non-destructive testing techniques using neutron imaging.",
        "01 Mar 2005 – 26 Jul 2011 | Principal Scientific Officer & Group Leader, NR Group, RNPD, INST. Managed applied research in neutron physics using 3 MW TRIGA MK-II research reactor.\n➤ Developed experimental methods that expanded applications of neutron radiography in industry\n01 Jul 1995 – 28 Feb 2005 | Senior Scientific Officer & Group Leader, NR Group, RNPD, INST. Oversaw reactor-based research and development in imaging techniques.\n➤ Coordinated collaborative projects and improved reactor utilization for applied science.\n09 May 1995 – 30 Jun 1995 | Senior Scientific Officer, RNP Division, INST. Focused on neutron-based experimental setups and data analysis.\n➤ Contributed to upgrades in experimental protocols within the division.\n16 Sep 1990 – 08 May 1995 | Scientific Officer, RNP Division, INST. Conducted research in reactor and neutron physics and supported lab operations.\n➤ Gained foundational experience in neutron beam experiments and facility operation.\nAdministrative Experience:\n25-09-2019 to 31-12-2020 | Director General, Atomic Energy Research Establishment (AERE), BAEC, Savar, Dhaka.\n03-03-2014 to 24-09-2019 | Director, Training Institute, AERE, BAEC, Savar, Dhaka.",
        "03-10-2011 to 18-11-2011 | Director In-Charge, Training Institute, AERE, Savar, Dhaka (in absence of the regular Director).\n01-07-1995 to 02-03-2014 | Group Leader, Neutron Radiography (NR) Group, Reactor and Neutron Physics Division (RNPD), INST, AERE, Savar, Dhaka.\nPrevious Teaching experience/Lectures delivered\nSL | Summary\n1. | Delivered a substantial number of lectures to participants of various training courses organized by the Training Institute of BAEC. Participants included scientists, university and college teachers, and defense personnel.\n2. | A series of lectures have been given to the students of different semester from Islamic University of Technology (IUT), Gazipur for their Industrial Training programme at the Institute of Nuclear Science and technology of BAEC.\n3. | Delivered lectures in the Basic Nuclear Orientation Course organized for newly recruited scientists by BAEC.\n4. | Lectures were delivered in the National Training Course on Radiographic Testing Level-2 in different years organized by Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) Academic Committee in collaboration with BAEC at the Atomic Energy Center (AEC), Dhaka.",
