        "Admission Requirements for BPharm (Hons) Program\nStudents must have a minimum aggregate GPA of 8.0 in S.S.C./ ‘O’ level or equivalent and H.S.C./ ‘A’ level or equivalent examinations (in a total scale of 10), but not less than GPA 3.5 (in a scale of 5) in each.\nAdditionally, students must pass H.S.C. with a minimum GPA of 3 in Physics and Mathematics, and 3.5 in Biology and Chemistry. In the case ‘A’ Level, students must pursue a minimum ‘C’ grade in Physics and Mathematics, and ‘B’ grade in Biology and Chemistry.\nStudents who have obtained less than a GPA of 3.00 in Mathematics / failed in Mathematics / did not take Mathematics in their HSC/ ‘A’ Level or equivalent examinations may be eligible for admission. However, they must complete one (1) additional 3-credit Mathematics course aligned with the BPharm curriculum.\nApplicants seeking admission to the BPharm program must complete the admission process within 3 (three) years from the year (Gregorian calendar) of publication of their HSC or equivalent examination results.\nProgram Details\nDuration | 4 Years\nCredit (Core) | 155\nCredit (Research Work) | 4\nCredit (Industrial Training) | 1\nTotal Credit for Graduation | 160",
        "Admission Requirements for MPharm (Master of Pharmacy) Program\nStudents seeking admission for the degree of MPharm should have passed BPharm (Honours) from any recognized University.\nThe student’s CGPA in the B.Pharm examination shall not be less than 2.50 (4-point scale).\nProgramme Details | Thesis Group | Non-thesis Group\nCredit (Core) | 24 | 30\nCredit (Research Work) | 7 | 0\nCredit (Viva Voce) | 1 | 2\nTotal Credit for Postgraduation | 32 | 32"
      ]
