      "chunks": [
        "The Center for Multidisciplinary Research and the Department of Microbiology, Gono Bishwabidyalay, jointly organized a seminar titled “Fungal Disease Starts Where Life Happens: Awareness, Prevention and Protection” on 16 September 2026 at Gono Bishwabidyalay.\nThe seminar featured two distinguished Keynote Speakers:\nProfessor Dr. Tanvir Rahman\nProfessor, Department of Microbiology and Hygiene, BAU\nDr. Tania Haque\nDermatologist & Venereologist, GSMC\nThe keynote sessions provided valuable insights into fungal diseases, their clinical and microbiological significance, prevention, and protective measures. The program brought together faculty members, researchers, and students, creating an engaging platform for scientific knowledge sharing and discussion.\nThe seminar reflects the commitment of the Center for Multidisciplinary Research and the Department of Microbiology to promoting scientific awareness and interdisciplinary learning in areas of importance to public health.\nTogether, advancing knowledge, awareness, prevention and protection."
