        "By: Dr. Parvez Ahmed\nBOOK\n1. Parvez Ahmed, Cologne Commentary on Space Law (Bangla Version), 2022 Kamrul Law Book House, Dhaka, Bangladesh.\nPEER REVIEWED ARTICLES\n1. ‘A Legal and Technological Study on Bangabandhu Satgellite-1’ (2019) Vol.12 Issue 2, Journal of Law, Islamic University, Bangladesh.\n2. ‘The UN Watercourses Convention and Its Significance in Teesta River Water Sharing between India and Bangladesh: A Critical Appraisal’ (2018) Vol. 12 Issue 1, The Islamic University Studies, Bangladesh.\n3. ‘Impact of IQAC for Ensuring Quality Education in Bangladesh in Digital Age: An Overview’ in Abhigyan Bhattacharjee (ed), Human Resource Management and Development in Digital Age-Some Sector Specific Perspective, (Mittal Publications, New Delhi, India 2018).\n4.‘Application of Identification Theory in the UK Courts and Its Efficacy in the Judiciary of Bangladesh for Corporate Homicide’ (2016) Volume 1, Issue 2, Uttara University Law Journal, Bangladesh.\n5.‘Protection of Workers in Workplaces: A Comparative Study of Labour Laws of the UK, the USA and Bangladesh, (2015) Volume 2 Issue 1, Green University Review of Social Sciences, Bangladesh.",
        "6. ‘The Law Relating to Adultery: A Critical Evaluation in Present Social Context’ (2014) Volume1 Issue 6 International Journal of Law and Legal Jurisprudence Studies (ISSN:2348-8212), India.\n7. ‘Corporate Civil and Criminal Liability and the Bangladesh Labour Act 2006: A Critical Evaluation’ (2013) Vol 4 no 1-2, Green University Review, Bangladesh.\n8. ‘Shareholder Activism and Protection of Minority Shareholders: Bangladesh Perspective’ (2010) Vol 6 No. 2, Journal of Islamic Education and Research, Islamic University, Bangladesh.\n9. ‘The Impact of ‘Ordre Public’ on Party Autonomy in International Commercial Arbitration: National and International Views’ accepted for publication in Rajshahi University Law Journal, Rajshahi University, Bangladesh.\n10. ‘Workplace Deaths and Injuries and their Prosecutions under Bangladeshi Laws: Weaknesses and Remedies’ (2011) Vol. 2 Issue: 05, SIU Studies Sylhet International University, Bangladesh.\n11.‘White Collar Crime and Its Practices in Education and Medical Sectors of Bangladesh’ (2007) Vol VII, Rajshahi University Law Review, Bangladesh.",
        "12. ‘State of Human Trafficking and Law and Policy in Bangladesh’ (2006) Vol. 6 No.2, Islamic University Studies, Bangladesh.\n13. ‘Restorative Justice: A Different Way of Dealing with Crime and Criminal’ (2006) Vol. 6 No.1 The Islamic University Studies, Bangladesh.\n14. “Triple Divorce: A Legal Analysis’ (2003) Vol. 4 No. 2, The Islamic University Studies, Bangladesh.\nCONFERENCE/SEMINAR PRESENTATIONS:\n1.‘Bangabandhu Satellite-1 after Five Years of Its Launch: A Review on Legal and Economic Perspective’ in Conference on Aviation and Space Law on 23 September 2023, BSMR Aviation and Aerospace University, Dhaka, Bangladesh.\n2.‘Protection of Consumers: A Comparative Legal Study between Bangladesh and Malaysia’ in International Conference on Innovation and Transformation for Development on 30 October 2022, Green University of Bangladesh, Dhaka, Bangladesh.\n3.‘Preservation of Space Environment under National and International Law’ in National Conference on Environmental Law and Policy on 23 July 2022, Green University of Bangladesh, Dhaka, Bangladesh.",
        "4. ‘Necessity of National Space Legislation after Bangabandhu Satellite-1’ in National Conference on Stakeholders’ Opinions before Launching of BS-2, 4 Sep 2019 Dhaka, Bangladesh.\n5.‘Protection of Interests of Developing Countries under the Outer Space Treaty’ in International Conference on Commercial Exploitation of Outer Space through Satellites: Prospects and Challenges, 22 Aug 2019, Green University of Bangladesh, Dhaka, Bangladesh.\n6. ‘Outer Space and Sustainable Development: A case Study on Bangladesh’ in International Conference on Space Law: Implications in Developing Countries, 16 Aug 2018, Green University of Bangladesh, Dhaka, Bangladesh.\n7. ‘Corporate Criminal Liability and Protection of Workers in the Garment Industries of Bangladesh’ in International Global Law and Policy Conference, 2 Jun 2018, Harvard Law School, Boston, MA, USA.\n8. ‘Role of Academic Institutions regarding Application of Remote Sensing Data for Water Management: Bangladesh Perspective’ in 4th United Nations International Conference on the Use of Space Technology for Water Management, 26 Feb-2 Mar 2018, Islamabad, Pakistan.",
        "9. ‘Combating Impunity for Frequent Corporate Homicides: Bangladesh Should Learn from Australia’ in Corporate Law Teachers’ Association Annual Conference 2018, La Trobe University, Australia.\n10. ‘Outer Space and Developing Countries’ on the theme ‘50 Years of Space Law-Space Law in 50 Years’ during the period of Directed Studies under the Hague Academy of International Law, 7 Sep 2017, the Hague, The Netherlands.\n11.‘Application of the ICT as Educational Tools and Its Impact on Career Development for University Faculty Members: An Empirical Study’ in International Seminar on Human Resource Management and Development in the Digital Age, 24 Jun 2017, Meghalaya, India.\n12. ‘UN Convention on the Law of the Non-Navigational Uses of International Watercourses, 1997 and its Compliance in Teesta River Water Sharing’ in International conference on Water Sharing in the SAARC Region: Legal Issues and Challenges, 26 March 2017, NALSAR University of Law, Hyderabad, India.",
        "13.‘Workplace Safety and Recent Casualties at Garment Factories in Bangladesh: Looking through the Lens of the Stakeholder Theory of Corporation and Islamic Law’ in 14th Asian Business Research Conference organised by World Business Institute (WBI), Australia 30 Dec 2016 in Dhaka, Bangladesh.\n14. ‘Liabilities of a company to its employees and the provisions of the Labour Act 2006: An Analysis’ Ph.D. Seminar Series, 10 Mar 2013 Islamic University, Bangladesh.\n15. ‘Laws of England on Corporate Civil and Criminal Liability: An Analysis, Ph.D. Seminar Series, 9 Mar 2013 Islamic University, Bangladesh.\nCONFERENCE/SEMINAR ATTENDED\n1. Joined Gujarat National Law University Space Law Conference as a Keynote Speaker on the 7the Edition of GNLU Air and Space Law Academy (GASLA 2022) from 26 September -30 September 2022.\n2. One Week Online International Faculty Development Program on Impact of Covid-19 on Legal Education and Legal Research – Way Forward organized by The N. J. Y. Centre for Post-Graduate Legal Research, ICFAI Law School, The ICFAI University Tripura (8-14 August, 2021).",
        "3. Virtual Workshop on the Space Technology Applications for Drought, Flood and Water Resources Management. Organized by United Nations/ Islamic Republic of Iran (9-11 August 2021).\n4. Space Economy: Africa In Focus organized by United Nations Office for Outer Space Affairs (virtual) (Wednesday, 30 June, 2021).\n5. Participated as panel discussant at the Dialogue with Academicians on ADR organised by Bangladesh International Arbitration Centre on 31 January 2019.\n6. Participated in a seminar on ‘National Consultation of Equal Opportunity for All: Towards an Anti-discrimination Legislation’ organised by NHRC and Law Commission Bangladesh on 30.03.2016 at International Conference Centre, CIRDAP, Dhaka.\n7. Attended a seminar on ‘International Human Rights Instrument on Indigenous People and Implementation in Bangladesh’ at Daffodil International University on 25 August 2015",
        "8. Participated in an International seminar on the Internet and Freedom of Expression as an academician on 25 January, 2014 at the Hotel Sarina, Plot 27, Road 17, Banani, Dhaka. The seminar was jointly organized by VOICE (Bangladesh), The internet democracy project (India), Internet Society Nepal (Nepal), Point of View (India) and Global Partners and Associates (the UK).\n9. Worked as a Resource Person for conducting a training course on Leadership & Conflict Management for the Rohingya Refugee Community implemented by United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) from 25 November to 02 December 2011 in Cox’s Bazaar, Bangladesh.\nBy: Thouhidul Islam\nCell : 01715 865098\nBy: Md. Lemon Hossen\nCell: 01751178080\nBy: Dr. Shahdeen Malik\nShahdeen Malik Profile\nAdjunct Professor",
        "Dr. Shahdeen Malik is an advocate of the Supreme Court of Bangladesh and head of chambers of Ergo Legal Counsel (ELC). ELC primarily focuses on a number of practice areas including but not limited to constitutional law, administrative law and election laws. Additionally, ELC litigates in a number of other areas which includes company and banking matters, criminal practice (primarily concerned with anti-corruption matters), family and personal law matters. Shahdeen Malik’s practice spans over two decades in the Supreme Court and the district court where he was enrolled in 2000 and 1996 respectively.\nOutside of legal practice, Shahdeen Malik is currently serving as an independent Director of Pubali Bank Ltd. Bangladesh, as a member of the Board of Trustees in Center for Policy Dialogue (CPD), and other organizations.\nOther than legal practice, Shahdeen Malik’s oeuvre of work has encompassed academia, research and policy. He had taught law in Dhaka University in the 1980s. He continues to teach as an adjunct faculty member in different universities. Previously, Shahdeen Malik had been the Director of School of Law, BRAC University (2005-2014).",
        "In addition to practice and academia, Shahdeen Malik has served as the Honorary Director of the Bangladesh Institute of Legal and International Affairs (BILIA) (2010-2019); and worked as a consultant for various international organizations such the United Nations and DFID (UK) etc. Shahdeen Malik’s research and scholarship has been published in a number of international journals in the USA, Netherlands, Germany, India and Bangladesh.\nBy: Tasnuva Rashid\nRashid T, Hossain S, and Amin MA. (2023). Child rights in Bangladesh: a comparative analysis on\nnational and international legal framework, Asian J. Soc. Sci. Leg. Stud., 5(6), 208-223.\nChild rights in Bangladesh_a comparative analysis on national and international legal framework\n1 2 3 next »"
